<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Aqueduct Loop (Highway 35 by Road 44; clockwise round Dog River Butte; Road 17 back over Raven Pass)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:215-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.373973" lon="-121.566853"><ele>1008.3</ele><name>Highway 35 at Road 44</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hwy35-road-44 (OSM node 33436785); confidence: high; pdf_page: 214; book_elev_ft: 3280; quote: All tours in this area are reached by skiing (or driving) uphill on Road 44 from Highway 35 ... (3,280 feet)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.413987" lon="-121.525820"><ele>1293.9</ele><name>Road 44, 200 yd south of the 44/1720 (today 44/17) junction: start of the loop</name><desc>source: OSM node 33444395 on Road 44, 249 m south of the junction (the nearest node to 200 yd); confidence: high; pdf_page: 217; quote: go to the junction of Roads 44 and 1720 at the south end of Brooks Meadow. Ski 200 yards south on Road 44, enter forest to the right (west), and locate the primitive road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.416990" lon="-121.533280"><ele>1334.6</ele><name>Old road (OSM Forest Road 1700-692) where Surveyor's Ridge Trail #688 crosses it</name><desc>source: OSM node 3708386319; 1700-692 keeps to the 4,300-4,350 ft contour along the butte's south side; confidence: low; pdf_page: 217; quote: Follow it as it circles the butte through solid forest.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.414962" lon="-121.540809"><ele>1331.0</ele><name>West end of Forest Road 1700-692, south-west side of Dog River Butte</name><desc>source: OSM node 3708386440 (end of the mapped road); confidence: low; pdf_page: 217</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.419000" lon="-121.543200"><ele>1280.8</ele><name>West side of Dog River Butte, about 4,250 ft</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM contour; no mapped way; confidence: low; pdf_page: 217; quote: At 1 mile there is a short, exciting downhill with a good runout.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.424000" lon="-121.540500"><ele>1270.5</ele><name>North-west side of Dog River Butte</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM; no mapped way; confidence: low; pdf_page: 217</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.425800" lon="-121.535500"><ele>1283.9</ele><name>North side of Dog River Butte</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM; no mapped way; confidence: low; pdf_page: 217</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.426436" lon="-121.527708"><ele>1298.5</ele><name>Surveyor's Ridge Trail #688 at the Super Connector Trail, north-east of the butte</name><desc>source: OSM node 3670602906; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 217</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.431580" lon="-121.531695"><ele>1297.0</ele><name>Side route to Raven Rock: #688 at the Super Connector, north of the butte</name><desc>source: OSM node 5328819164; #688 (way 945297131) goes on north to Road 1700-680 toward Raven Rock (216-2's end, OSM viewpoint 'Mt Hood East Side View'); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 217; quote: At 2.7 miles from the start of the old road, a side route leads to Raven Rock.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.429438" lon="-121.527979"><ele>1293.1</ele><name>Road 17 at the Super Connector, end of the old road</name><desc>source: OSM node 33434852 on Forest Road 17; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 217; quote: To complete the loop, ski to Road 17 which is followed southward over a high point, Raven Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.416224" lon="-121.525894"><ele>1302.4</ele><name>Road 44 / Road 17 junction (the book's 44/1720 junction), south end of Brooks Meadow</name><desc>source: OSM node 33437099, as in 215-1 and 216-2; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 217; book_elev_ft: 4280; quote: then along the west side of Brooks meadow 1.5 miles from the end of the old road to the junction of Roads 44/1720.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.373973" lon="-121.566853"><ele>1008.3</ele><name>Highway 35 at Road 44</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hwy35-road-44 (OSM node 33436785); confidence: high; pdf_page: 214; book_elev_ft: 3280</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Aqueduct Loop (Highway 35 by Road 44; clockwise round Dog River Butte; Road 17 back over Raven Pass)</name><desc>1. Highway 35 at Road 44 -&gt; Road 44, 200 yd south of the 44/1720 (today 44/17) junction: start of the loop: osm (high), 5.07 mi | 2. Road 44, 200 yd south of the 44/1720 (today 44/17) junction: start of the loop -&gt; Old road (OSM Forest Road 1700-692) where Surveyor's Ridge Trail #688 crosses it: straight (low), 0.42 mi | 3. Old road (OSM Forest Road 1700-692) where Surveyor's Ridge Trail #688 crosses it -&gt; West end of Forest Road 1700-692, south-west side of Dog River Butte: osm (low), 0.52 mi | 4. West end of Forest Road 1700-692, south-west side of Dog River Butte -&gt; West side of Dog River Butte, about 4,250 ft: straight (low), 0.30 mi | 5. West side of Dog River Butte, about 4,250 ft -&gt; North-west side of Dog River Butte: straight (low), 0.37 mi | 6. North-west side of Dog River Butte -&gt; North side of Dog River Butte: straight (low), 0.27 mi | 7. North side of Dog River Butte -&gt; Surveyor's Ridge Trail #688 at the Super Connector Trail, north-east of the butte: straight (low), 0.38 mi | 8. Surveyor's Ridge Trail #688 at the Super Connector Trail, north-east of the butte -&gt; Side route to Raven Rock: #688 at the Super Connector, north of the butte: osm (medium), 0.46 mi | 9. Side route to Raven Rock: #688 at the Super Connector, north of the butte -&gt; Road 17 at the Super Connector, end of the old road: osm (medium), 0.24 mi | 10. Road 17 at the Super Connector, end of the old road -&gt; Road 44 / Road 17 junction (the book's 44/1720 junction), south end of Brooks Meadow: osm (high), 1.16 mi | 11. Road 44 / Road 17 junction (the book's 44/1720 junction), south end of Brooks Meadow -&gt; Highway 35 at Road 44: osm (high), 5.23 mi</desc>
